def is_prime(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return False
    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):
        if n % i == 0:
            return False
    return True
```
This function works by checking if the number is divisible by any number from 2 up to the square root of the number. If it is divisible by any of these numbers, it is not prime. If it is not divisible by any, it is prime.
